I was minding my own business when a knife came sailing through a doorway 
just next to me. A goblin came wandering in after his knife and I realised 
he had thrown it because I was displaced (via cloak) to that location.

This has changed my ideas about displacement, because I had always thought 
it just displaced you from the point of view of monsters who could already 
see you, like an illusion cast on each monster looking at you. I wasn't in 
that goblin's line of sight, though, so clearly you can "appear" to a 
monster via displacement even if it couldn't see you otherwise. Interesting!

